const report=`# Desktop Atlas source-runtime measurements\n\n26 October 2026 · exact native a01/05215efe · sealed stock build 557files · loopback only\n\n## Core Web Vitals summary\n\n| Local lab measurement | Whole-body bones | Thorax, all available systems | Interpretation |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| LCP | 708ms | 718ms | Good within this observed run; whole-body LCP was loading/recovery text, not 3D model readiness |\n| INP | Not produced in the load-only trace | 28ms for the explode End-key interaction | Good observed interaction; not field/p75 acceptance |\n| CLS | 0.00 | 0.00 | No measured layout shift within these traces |\n\nRatings use [Google's Web Vitals definitions](https://web.dev/articles/vitals). A local lab result does not establish real-user percentile performance. CPU throttling1x, no network throttling, 1280x900 and later1440x900, device scale1, actual AMD Radeon Direct3D11 WebGL renderer. The same integration source is used by the Atlas modules; this independent native run does not establish signed-in Website acceptance.\n\n## Actual rendering and interaction\n\n- The initial whole-body scope enabled bones(203), not every one of the1104available catalogue entries. Actual WebGL anatomy was viewed. Two keyboard rotations produced24ms Event Timing entries; a3second browser-rAF sample had18msmedian/18.1msp95 and no interval above50ms. This is browser cadence, not a claim of continuously rendered3D FPS.\n- Thorax enabled all158available entries across its supported systems; absent nervous geometry remained disabled.21model resource entries were observed, including both revalidated assets and fresh transfers. First instrumented WebGL draw was1.345s after navigation; it is not a certified all-model-readiness marker. Initialization included a328mslong task. The3second explode sample had17.4msmedian/17.6msp95 browser intervals, maximum23.1ms, and no interval above50ms. Trace INP28ms and Event Timing32ms are separately preserved observations.\n- Stage3 chest-wall dissection displayed two source labels and allowed selection. A2second settled selected-view window issued zero WebGL draw calls. Labels stayed within canvas bounds. The field initially named selectedHeading matched a hidden practice heading; it is not evidence of an incorrect visible selection. Actual snapshot showed the intercostal selection.\n- The3xautomatic tour was observed at step1, then step5, then the final left pulmonary artery stop with playback ended, without manual Next activation. Intermediate steps2–4 were not individually captured. Initial3second samples happened during static dwells and correctly had zero WebGL draws.\n- Keyboard Back from the final stop exercised an actual camera transition:151of169rAFwindows contained rendering,2416draw calls,18msmedian/18.1msp95 and22.36msmaximum interval over3seconds; no interval exceeded50ms. This bounded sample is not a whole-tour smoothness or GPU-frame benchmark.\n- Exiting restored the Dissect workspace. Settled1440layout had an882pxcanvas, no document scroll/overflow and independent left/right panel scrolling. The immediate post-resize1440observation is retained but superseded by the settled after-tour layout. Approximate observed Chrome JS heap ranged from84.6MB at whole-body capture to160.8MB at thorax capture; these are neither total process RAM nor GPU-memory measurements. No active-context loss was observed.\n\n## Top issues and remaining scope\n\n1. No latency repair is justified by these bounded results. Render-blocking/image-delivery insights estimated zero LCP/FCP impact, so no speculative dependency or image change was made.\n2. Initial328msmain-thread work warrants targeted follow-up if broader cold/slow-network acceptance exposes a problem. This run contains cached/revalidated resources; do not call it a complete cold-cache or internet delivery test.\n3. Dense8-label scenes, whole-body with all systems, other regions/specimens, different devices, cancellation/retry/context-loss recovery and authenticated Website/PACS-linked journeys remain unverified here. UX-03 can move from open to partial only; its full acceptance remains unchanged.\n\n## Codebase and provenance\n\nReact/vinext, Three.js/React Three Fiber and the existing source-bound production artifacts were used. No production code, assets, masks, clinical teaching, licence, dependency, auth, entitlement or normal-preview configuration changed. The legacy Three.Clock warning was observed; no performance impact was established and no package upgrade was made. All6410source paths,215public assets and557build artifacts remain byte-exact after QA.\n\nThe initial admission looked only at a retained failed build. Its report is preserved; ADMISSION_V2 authenticates the later successful balanced build. The Chrome tool refused an F-drive raw trace path; supported inline insights were used with no permission changes. Two metadata-write commands refused trace text containing quote characters; those writes never ran, then safe base64 payloads saved the returned text locally. Raw trace files and screenshot files were not saved. All seven owned preview processes and page28are closed; only the existing blank Chrome page remains. No review/data endpoint, scan, identifier or clinical PACS was used. No private data is uploaded.\n`;
